 do I play Baccarat?\nThe objective of Baccarat is to guess\nwhich hand, out of the two hands||the dealer deals, is closest to \"9\".\nAll you have to do is place your bet||on the hand you think will win.\nAt the beginning of the game,\nthe dealer deals 2 cards to both||the \"PLAYER\" and the \"BANKER\".\nThe cards are turned up in order from||the \"PLAYER\" to the \"BANKER\"\nand in some cases a third card may be dealt.\nWhen the third or final cards are turned up,||the hand closest to 9 wins.\n10s and face cards equal 0,{PA:10}||and Aces equal 1.{PA:10}\nIf the sum of two or more cards||equal 10 or higher,\n10 will be subtracted from the total.\nWhen the winner and the loser is decided,||if you had bet on the winner,\nthe payout will be double the amount.\nYou can also bet on a \"Tie\".\nIf the \"PLAYER\" and the \"BANKER\" tie, the||payout will be 8 times the amount you bet.\nIn this case, the chips placed on either the||\"PLAYER\" or the \"BANKER\" will be returned.\nThe percentage of a tie is very low,||therefore the payout is quite large.\nWell, {PA:10}that's the basics.\nBaccarat is a pretty difficult game||to grasp at first, so would you like\na more detailed explanation?\nYes, please.\nLet me explain the rules pertaining to||the third card, which happens to be\nthe most complicated part of Baccarat.\nIf both the \"PLAYER\" and the \"BANKER\"||have a total other than 8 or 9\nthe game will continue\nFirst off, I'll tell you about what happens||when the total of the 2 cards of\nthe \"PLAYER\" equals 6 or 7.\nIn this case, the player cannot||draw a third card.\nAlso, the \"BANKER\" can only draw||when their total equals 5 or less.\nIf this happens, the game is over.\nNext, I'll tell you about what happens||when the total of the 2 cards of\nthe \"PLAYER\" equals 5 or less.\nIn this case, the player must draw||a third card.\nWhether the \"BANKER\" can draw a third card||or not depends on the total of the \"BANKER\"\nand the third card drawn by the \"PLAYER\".\nOkay,{PA:10} let me explain step-by-step.\nIf the total of the \"BANKER\" equals 7,||they cannot draw a third card.\nIf the total of the \"BANKER\" equals 6||and the third card drawn by the \"PLAYER\"\nis 6 or 7...\nthe \"BANKER\" draws a third card.\nIf the total of the \"BANKER\" equals 5 and||the third card drawn by the \"PLAYER\" is...\n4, 5, 6 or 7,||the \"BANKER\" draws a third card.\nIf the total of the \"BANKER\" equals 4 and||the third card drawn by the \"PLAYER\" is...\n2, 3 ,4, 5, 6 or 7,||the \"BANKER\" draws a third card.\nIf the total of the \"BANKER\" equals 3||and the third card drawn by the \"PLAYER\"\nis anything other than 8...||the \"BANKER\" draws a third card.\nIf the total of the \"BANKER\" equals 1 or 2,||the \"BANKER\" must draw a third card.\nAt this point, {PA:10}the winner and||the loser will be decided.\nHonestly,{PA:10} I don't think you can fully||understand this game\nwith just an explanation.\nTry a few games, {PA:10}and if you still don't||understand, come back and ask me again.\nGood luck."
